  "result": "I fixed the option order in `--help` in `src/click/formatting.py`. The full test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n`join_options` sorted each option's names with `reverse=True`. That put the long name first, as in `--verbose, -v`. Click normally lists the short name first, as in `-v, --verbose`. I removed `reverse=True`.\n\nI didn't check the `--help` output by hand, and I didn't add a test for the ordering.\n\nI looked at other places that could produce a \"weird order\" and they were fine. The order options are listed in comes from `get_params` and `format_options`. The reversal of decorator-applied params in `decorators.py` is correct.\n\nIf you meant something else by \"weird order\", such as the order of the options in the list rather than the order of names within one option, tell me and I'll look again.",
